---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Suslify | Why We Built It"
  description="Suslify was built to solve a simple problem: too many people have usable items they don't need, and too many charities need exactly those items but can't reach donors."
>
  <Header />

  <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-white pt-20 pb-16 md:pt-28">
    <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="absolute -top-32 -right-32 w-[500px] h-[500px] rounded-full bg-brand-100/50 blur-3xl"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="relative max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5">

      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-600 mb-4">About</p>
      <h1 class="text-5xl sm:text-6xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 mb-8 leading-tight">
        Why we built<br />
        <span class="text-brand-500">Suslify.</span>
      </h1>

      <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none text-slate-600 leading-relaxed space-y-6 text-[1.05rem]">
        <p>
          The idea for Suslify started with a simple observation: people get rid
          of good things every day: furniture, clothes, appliances, books. A
          lot of it ends up in landfill. Meanwhile, charities and families who
          could use those exact items have no easy way to find them.
        </p>

        <p>
          Existing options are fragmented. You post on Facebook Marketplace, you
          email a charity and wait, you drop things at a collection point without
          knowing if they'll actually get used. There's no single place to post
          what you have, see who needs it, communicate, and confirm it arrived.
        </p>

        <p>
          Suslify is that place. We built it to make the connection between
          donors and charities as simple as possible. Posting an item takes
          under a minute, messaging is built in, and every donation is tracked
          from listing to pickup so nothing falls through the cracks.
        </p>

        <p>
          It's free for everyone. Donors, recipients, charities. No one pays to
          give or to receive. That's not a promotion; it's the point.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 p-7 bg-brand-50 rounded-2xl border border-brand-100">
        <p class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">Got a question or want to partner?</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-4">We'd love to hear from you.</p>
        <a href="mailto:suslifysupport@gmail.com"
           class="inline-flex bg-brand-500 hover:bg-brand-600 text-white font-bold text-sm px-5 py-2.5 rounded-full transition-all shadow-md shadow-brand-500/20">
          suslifysupport@gmail.com
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
